
DO NOT USE THIS TOOL

npm's fundamental flaw is that it will add a lot
of files in the local node_modules directory, and
there is no sane way to prevent massive bloat.
Use yarn instead.

By default, npm will download GiBs of crap
into $HOME.  You can change the location with:

NPM_CONFIG_CACHE
NPM_CONFIG_LOGS_DIR
NPM_CONFIG_NPA_CACHE

You can also use `npm config set cache /p/a/t/h --global`
to modify ~/.npmrc.  I'm not sure how that plays with the
log or NPA cache
